4.2 Add ec2-user to Docker Group
sudo usermod -aG docker ec2-user
Log out & log back in so group membership applies.
Verify:
groups
You should see docker included.
4.3 Create Mosquitto Config & Data Directories
mkdir -p ~/mosquitto/config
mkdir -p ~/mosquitto/data
mkdir -p ~/mosquitto/log
4.4 Create Basic Mosquitto Config
nano ~/mosquitto/config/mosquitto.conf
Paste:
listener 1883
allow_anonymous true
persistence true
persistence_location /mosquitto/data/
log_dest file /mosquitto/log/mosquitto.log
Save.
4.5 Run Mosquitto Broker Using Docker
Use the exact working command you already executed:
docker run -d \
  --name mosquitto \
  -p 1883:1883 \
  -v ~/mosquitto/config/mosquitto.conf:/mosquitto/config/mosquitto.conf \
  -v ~/mosquitto/data:/mosquitto/data \
  -v ~/mosquitto/log:/mosquitto/log \
  eclipse-mosquitto
Check the container:
docker ps
Inspect logs:
docker logs mosquitto

4.6 Verify Mosquitto is Listening
sudo ss -lntp | grep 1883
Expected:
LISTEN 0 128 0.0.0.0:1883 ...
